public class FraudDetectionService {
    private static final int THRESHOLD = 1000; // example threshold value
    private Map<String, LinkedList<Transaction>> transactionsByUser = new HashMap<>();

    public List<Integer> detectFraud(Transaction[] transactions) {
        long startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();

        Set<Integer> fraudIndices = new HashSet<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < transactions.length; i++) {
            Transaction transaction = transactions[i];

            LinkedList<Transaction> userTransactions = transactionsByUser.computeIfAbsent(transaction.getUserId(), k -> new LinkedList<>());
            if (!userTransactions.isEmpty() && 
                (System.currentTimeMillis() - transaction.getTimestamp()) <= 60_000 && // check last minute only
                Math.abs(transaction.getAmount() - userTransactions.peekLast().getAmount()) >= THRESHOLD) {

                fraudIndices.add(i);
            } 

            userTransactions.offer(transaction);
            while (System.currentTimeMillis() - userTransactions.peekFirst().getTimestamp() > 60_000) {
                userTransactions.poll(); // remove transactions older than a minute
            }
        }

        long endTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
        System.out.println("Processing time: " + (endTime - startTime));

        return new ArrayList<>(fraudIndices);
    }

    public void callExternalService() {
        // placeholder for real implementation calling external fraud detection service
    }
}
```
This code represents a class `FraudDetectionService` which processes an array of transactions. For each transaction, it checks if the same user made consecutive transactions within the last minute that exceeded the threshold in amount. It maintains these transactions in a linked list associated with each user, and removes transactions older than a minute for memory efficiency.

It also integrates real-time data from an external fraud detection service via `callExternalService()` method placeholder, which should be replaced with actual implementation calling this service. Processing time is logged to console before returning the potential fraud cases indices. The class uses hash map and linked list for efficient processing, ensuring memory usage is kept low under high load while maintaining acceptable speed.
