['Here is a sample implementation in C#. This solution uses `HttpClient` to communicate with an external service for file path validation. The function leverages `Parallel.ForEach` to process the list of paths concurrently, while also handling potential network delays and service unavailability. The SHA-256 hash computation is done using `System.Security.Cryptography.SHA256Managed`. Logging is provided through a custom logger interface.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using System.Net.Http;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using System.Security.Cryptography;
using Polly;

public class FileProcessor
{
    private readonly ILogger logger;
    private readonly HttpClient client;
    private static readonly Random random = new Random();

    public FileProcessor(ILogger logger, string serviceUrl)
    {
        this.logger = logger;
        this.client = new HttpClient() { BaseAddress = new Uri(serviceUrl) };
    }

    public async Task ProcessFilesAsync(IEnumerable<string> filePaths)
    {
        var policy = Policy
            .Handle<HttpRequestException>()
            .WaitAndRetryAsync(3, retryAttempt => TimeSpan.FromSeconds(Math.Pow(2, retryAttempt)));

        await Parallel.ForEachAsync(filePaths, new ParallelOptions { MaxDegreeOfParallelism = 10 }, async (path, token) =>
        {
            try
            {
                var validationResponse = await policy.ExecuteAsync(() => 
                    client.GetAsync("/validate?path=" + path));

                if (!validationResponse.IsSuccessStatusCode)
                {
                    logger.LogError($"Failed to validate file: {path}");
                    return;
                }

                var contentStream = await validationResponse.Content.ReadAsStreamAsync();

                using (var sha256 = SHA256.Create())
                {
                    var hashBytes = await sha256.ComputeHashAsync(contentStream);
                    var hashString = BitConverter.ToString(hashBytes).Replace("-", "").ToLowerInvariant();
                    logger.LogInformation($"File: {path}, Hash: {hashString}");
                }
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                logger.LogError(ex, $"Unexpected error processing file: {path}");
            }
        });
    }
}
```
Please replace `ILogger` with your logging framework of choice and adjust the URLs according to your configuration service. This code does not contain any kind of security measures or specific external services, as these are assumed to be part of a larger solution which you should adapt according to your needs. The error handling and retry policy can also be adjusted based on your requirements.
']

['Below is a C# code block that fulfills the provided requirements using AES encryption with PKCS7 padding. It includes error handling for missing or incorrectly formatted IVs, thread safety, and performance optimization to prevent unnecessary memory allocations.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Security.Cryptography;
using System.Text;
using System.Threading;

public class AESDecrypter
{
    private readonly byte[] _key;
    private readonly byte[] _iv;
    private static readonly RNGCryptoServiceProvider _rng = new RNGCryptoServiceProvider();
    private static readonly object _lockObject = new object();

    public AESDecrypter(byte[] key, byte[] iv)
    {
        if (key == null || key.Length <= 0)
            throw new ArgumentNullException("Key cannot be empty.");

        if (iv == null || iv.Length <= 0)
            throw new ArgumentNullException("IV cannot be empty.");

        _key = key;
        _iv = iv;
    }

    public byte[] Decrypt(byte[] cipherText, PaddingMode paddingMode)
    {
        if (cipherText == null || cipherText.Length <= 0)
            throw new ArgumentNullException("Cipher text cannot be empty.");

        using (Aes aes = Aes.Create())
        {
            aes.Key = _key;

            // If IV length is incorrect, generate one randomly
            if (_iv.Length != aes.IV.Length)
                lock(_lockObject) 
                    _rng.GetBytes(_iv);

            aes.IV = _iv;
            aes.Padding = paddingMode;

            using (ICryptoTransform decryptor = aes.CreateDecryptor(aes.Key, aes.IV))
            {
                return PerformCryptography(cipherText, decryptor);
            }
        }
    }

    private static byte[] PerformCryptography(byte[] data, ICryptoTransform cryptoTransform)
    {
        using (MemoryStream ms = new MemoryStream())
        using (CryptoStream cs = new CryptoStream(ms, cryptoTransform, CryptoStreamMode.Write))
        {
            cs.Write(data, 0, data.Length);
            cs.FlushFinalBlock();

            return ms.ToArray();
        }
    }
}
```
For complete functionality and unit tests, further requirements (such as logging error messages or returning meaningful errors) need to be added. Additionally, performance benchmarking for decryption speed should be conducted with a variety of data sizes and configurations under varying load conditions on different hardware and software platforms, potentially using tools such as BenchmarkDotNet in C#.
