int main() {
    float *numbers;
    NFAPI_RX_PDU_T **pduList;
    int size;

    processInput(&numbers, &pduList, &size);

    float average = computeAverage(numbers, size);
    printf("Average: %.2f\n", average);

    // Print PDU list
    for (int i = 0; i < size; ++i) {
        printf("RNTI: %d, Signal Strength: %.2f dB\n", pduList[i]->RNTI, pduList[i]->SIGNAL_STRENGTH_TAG);
    }

    // Free memory allocated for numbers and PDU list
    free(numbers);
    for (int i = 0; i < size; ++i) {
        free(pduList[i]);
    }
    free(pduList);

    return 0;
}
```
This code first declares a structure `NFAPI_RX_PDU_T` which will be used to store the read numbers. The function `computeAverage` is defined to calculate the average of an array of floats. It also defines `processInput` that reads float numbers from standard input and stores them in an array. For each number, it allocates a new `NFAPI_RX_PDU_T` structure with a randomly generated signal strength within a certain range.
