<?php

use Memcached;
use RuntimeException;

class StringGenerator {
    private $memcached;
    private $salt;
    private $configSettings;

    public function __construct() {
        $this->memcached = new Memcached();
        $this->memcached->addServer('localhost', 11211);

        $this->fetchConfigSettingsFromEnvironmentVariable();
        if (empty($this->configSettings)) {
            throw new RuntimeException('Failed to fetch configuration settings');
        }

        $this->salt = $this->configSettings['SALT'];
    }

    private function fetchConfigSettingsFromEnvironmentVariable() {
        // replace this with actual implementation fetching from env var or DB
        $this->configSettings = [
            'SALT' => getenv('APP_SALT') ?: null,
        ];
    }

    public function generateUniqueRandomString($length) {
        $pattern = '/^(?=.*[a-z])(?=.*[A-Z])(?=.*\d)(?=.*[\W_])/';

        do {
            $str = $this->generateSecureSaltedHash('', true);
            // ensure no consecutive characters are the same
            for ($i = 0; $i < strlen($str) - 1; ++$i) {
                if ($str[$i] === $str[$i + 1]) {
                    $str = null;
                    break;
                }
            }
        } while (!preg_match($pattern, $str));

        return substr($str, 0, $length);
    }

    public function generateSecureSaltedHash($inputStr) {
        $key = $this->memcached->get('secure_hash');

        if (!$key) {
            $key = password_hash(uniqid(mt_rand(), true), PASSWORD_DEFAULT);
            $this->memcached->set('secure_hash', $key, 3600); // cache for 1 hour
        }

        return hash_hmac('sha256', $inputStr . $this->salt, $key);
    }
}
```

This code fetches the salt value from an environment variable and uses it to generate a secure salted hash. It also uses Memcached for caching mechanism and ensures that no consecutive characters are the same in the generated string. This function may not be entirely optimized for high-frequency requests, as memcached usage can introduce latency. But this implementation is simple and efficient considering the above points. In a real-world application, it would require further optimizations for better performance handling high-frequency requests.
"]

